        "superseded_justification": "Judge accepted intrinsic upstream ETL loss: for 3,182 of 39,534 ARB rows (8.049%), fhir_medication_request.sql:43-44 obtains prescription endpoints but :172-177 omits MedicationRequest.dispenseRequest.validityPeriod for incomplete or reversed intervals, yielding unrecoverable NULL start/stop values. authoredOn at :55,124 is pharmacy entry time, and medication_prescriptions.sql:19-58 plus medication_mix.sql:27-53,64-85 preserve no endpoints. The candidate's direct and mix branches, multiplicity, exact filters, identifier joins, and TIMESTAMP_NTZ parsing are correct; no alternate FHIR path can recover the oracle timestamps. Unkeyed comparison had paired 3,182 only_candidate NULL tuples and 3,182 only_oracle timestamp tuples, with matching schema and row count. divergent_dependencies(arb)=[]; no retry warranted.",
